      "id": 333713,
      "username": "brian_pond",
      "name": "Brian Pond",
      "created_at": "2022-08-08T17:48:17.429Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Customizing the options for a ‘Select’ DocField is definitely allowed in v13.8.  I just tested.</p>\n<p>I don’t have a production environment on a higher version.  But I have a few development environments.  I’ll try to upgrade one of those to v13.28, and see if I can duplicate.</p>\n<p>Is the <code>\"You can't set options for field ...\"</code> the <em>precise</em> text?<br>\nIf so, should be possible to search the Python code for this phrase.  Identify the file name.  Then review its git commits, to learn exactly when this change was introduced.</p>",
