    {
      "id": 333717,
      "username": "brian_pond",
      "name": "Brian Pond",
      "created_at": "2022-08-08T18:11:44.309Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Ahhh, I see; thanks!  The initial commit was for v14.  At some point, it must have been backported into v13.  <img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/+1.png?v=12\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>For what it’s worth, I agree with this change.  One of my customers once broke their ERPNext, by adding new Options for DocTypes like Journal Entries and Sales Invoices.  This change prevents such problems.</p>",
